  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Place the fixed Gemini safety policy in GenerateContentConfig.system_instruction and send only labeled serialized synthetic data through user contents without duplicating the policy.",
    "Preserve the combined 128 KiB input limit, zero-or-one-call behavior, no-tools boundary, structured output, evidence validation, sanitized failures, deterministic fallback, and all existing public API behavior.",
    "Add adversarial tests proving instruction/data role separation, absence of environment values, no tool configuration, and zero provider calls when the combined input limit is exceeded.",
    "Commit a fully resolved Python 3.12-compatible dependency lock with SHA-256 artifact hashes and prove a clean pip --require-hashes installation.",
    "Run a pinned dependency audit as a required project security check and CI gate that fails on known applicable advisories or audit errors without application credentials.",
    "Pass project/task/report/OpenAPI validation, backend tests, agentic tests, dependency consistency, dependency audit, secret baseline, and source-dataset immutability checks.",
    "Do not change the public API contract, frontend, database, dataset, or approved local synthetic-only product scope."
  ],
  "created_by": "human"
}
